  "description": "GPS receiver with a Modbus slave: position, altitude, speed, course, time and date, GPS quality and satellites",
  "revision": 1,
  "source": "Exemys, GPS-110-MB-PS User's Manual, Rev. 3",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "GPS-110-MB-PS User's Manual",
      "version": "Rev. 3",
      "url": "https://www.exemys.com/beta/docs/english/GPS-MB-PS_UM_E.pdf",
      "note": "chapter Modbus registers",
      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "sha256": "31038941222a104b66332fc495110fa099708be0224619c17ad01650744545b7"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus slave on its serial port and over Ethernet (Modbus TCP); the Modbus slave ID is set in the configuration.",
    "Main registers and alternative registers (latitude and longitude in degrees, minutes and a 7-digit fraction, date and time in separate fields) are both listed.",
    "Register numbers are those of the manual (40001 is the first holding register), counted from 1 (address_base 1).",
    "32-bit values are two registers, the first holding the lower part and the second the upper part (low word first).",
    "Values the source does not send read as 0. Latitude and longitude are degrees multiplied by 10,000,000 (signed); ASCII registers hold the character code.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "tcp+rtu",
  "port": 502,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "little",
  "address_base": 1,
  "x_status": "official",
